# Implement authoritative vector geometry

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation evidence covers typed structures only, unless
explicitly stated otherwise; the finite contract is not rendered output.

Generate layout boxes, stroke centerlines, expanded ink contours, equations,
rules, tables, and diagram paths with physical units and semantic provenance.

Current executable evidence now centralizes those seven authoritative vector
primitive families. Every primitive structurally carries caller-owned geometry
and semantic provenance, while page geometry retains caller-owned physical
bounds and composition order. A read-only provenance projection returns the
exact composition-order primitive indices owned by one semantic origin without
interpreting or mutating geometry.

An exhaustive 4,096-mask oracle crosses semantic-origin membership over twelve
ordered primitives while cycling all seven primitive families. It requires exact
composition-order indices, an empty result for an absent origin, and byte-for-
byte-equivalent page value semantics before and after projection. Geometry
generation, physical unit vocabulary, contour expansion, tessellation,
rasterization, material behavior, PDF, and live-motion projection remain open.

## Finite one-page physical-vector authority contract

**Inputs:** an accepted A4 page revision, measured semantic layout boxes,
stroke centerlines, admitted figures, table/equation/diagram geometry, and
stable semantic owner IDs. **Outputs:** an ordered vector page in millimeters
with explicit bounds and owner mappings, or a blocking geometry diagnostic.
The same vector authority must feed Preview, Final, PDF and physical planning;
paint and texture never edit its coordinates.

**First-release geometry:** use an A4 `210 x 297 mm` page with a declared
writable rectangle `x=20..190`, `y=20..277`. Every vector primitive has
finite coordinates, measured width/height where applicable, explicit clip
owner and a source identity. The seven admitted primitive families are
`LayoutBox`, `StrokeCenterline`, `ExpandedInkContour`, `RulePath`, `Equation`,
`Table` and `DiagramPath`. A placed image remains linked to its original
asset bytes and measured clip rectangle, rather than falsely becoming a
fully editable vector object. A converted line-art image is a distinct
source-linked `DiagramPath` proposal.

**Worked composition (one page):**

| Primitive | Geometry in mm | Semantic origin |
| --- | --- | --- |
| LayoutBox | `(20,20,170,40)` | Page section `sec1` |
| StrokeCenterline | `(22,32)` to `(52,32)` | Text span `t1` |
| ExpandedInkContour | 0.25 mm around `t1` | Text span `t1` |
| RulePath | `(20,60)` to `(190,60)` | Rule `r1` |
| Equation | Box `(20,70,90,20)` | Formula `e1` |
| Table | 2 x 2 grid at `(20,95,100,40)` | Table `tab1` |
| DiagramPath | Clipped `x=130..190,y=95..155` | Figure `f1` |

**Clipping and order:** keep caller-approved composition order and exact
source-to-vector provenance, including every table cell, mathematical symbol
and original figure identity. Derived contours may expand around centerlines
but cannot change centerline contact order. A clip must be an explicit
physical rectangle, not a CSS viewport. A stroke that leaves the writable
rectangle fails output preflight even when a digital preview could paint it.

**Refusal example:** an equation path contains NaN, a table border extends to
x=195 mm, or a source image has no approved clip or decoder. Preserve the
original semantic notebook and return the offending owner/coordinates;
never truncate, normalize, or silently recolor. Unsupported raster-only
shadow/texture effects remain separate material requests, not vector claims.

**Assumptions and limits:** the repository has seven typed primitive families,
ordered page provenance and read-only owner projection, but not the geometry
generator, physical units enforcement, path expansion, clipping renderer,
PDF encoding or motion projection. The example is a theoretical vector plan,
not an actually emitted render surface.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for typed vector/page provenance; theoretical for
  geometric generation and physical path validation, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one seven-primitive A4 page, measured clips/owners,
  deterministic composition and invalid-geometry refusals.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** authoritatively generated strokes,
  vector paint, table/equation tessellation, image decoding, PDF or live paths.
